## Common Rules (Both Types)

### Double Row (前後2列)
All calculations use **2 rows** (front + back)

### Sharing Principle (共用)
Adjacent spans share the post/frame at the boundary:
- Post/Frame positions per wall = `spans + 1`

### Base Yokoji / Negarami (根がらみ) — BASE LEVEL ONLY
- Span direction: `N × 2` (front + back)
- Width direction: `N+1` (every post position)

### Anchi Layout by Width
- 600mm → 1 full anchi (500mm wide)
- 900mm → 1 full anchi (500mm) + 1 half anchi (240mm)
- 1200mm → 2 full anchi (500mm each)

### Stair Sets (階段セット)
- Each access point is a complete vertical stair tower
- Stair replaces 1 full anchi per level per access point (for width ≥ 900mm)
- For 600mm width: extended bay pattern (no anchi removal)

### Corner Rule (足場コーナー詳細図) — BOTH Kusabi AND Wakugumi
At every polygon corner where two walls meet:
1. **300mm overrun**: Scaffold run along each wall = **wallLength + 300mm**
2. **Span layout (closed polygon)**: `[first_span_along_wall, ...middle_spans, terminal_corner_span]`
   - Kusabi: first = **1800mm**, terminal into corner = **600mm**; middle = wallLength − 2100mm (standard spans)
   - Wakugumi: first = **1829mm** (6尺), terminal = **610mm**; middle = wallLength − 2139mm
   - Very short walls fall back to legacy `[600,…,600]` / `[610,…,610]`
3. **Post sharing**: Inner posts of the terminal 600/610 bay are reused by the next wall’s first span (continuous deck)
4. **Backend**: `fitSpansToWallLengthWithCorner()` / `fitSpansToWallLengthWithCornerWakugumi()`
5. **3D view**: `buildWallScaffold()` with corner start shift + shared corner post; `flushDeckAtCornerEnd` on terminal bay
6. Example (kusabi): Wall 10,200mm → spans = [1800, 1800, 1800, 1800, 900, 600] (sum = 10,500 = wall + 300)

### Jack Base
- Range: 0~300mm adjustable
- Count only, no size spec in quotation

### PATTANKO (パッタンコ)
- Small filler plank used at corners where walls meet, to close the gap when spans do not align.
- 3D view: rendered at each corner, per level, bridging inner and outer rows (2 per corner per level).
- BOM: can be counted as corner fill (e.g. 2 × corners × levels) if quoted separately.

## Output
1. **足場材料見積書 (Excel)** — Per-wall columns + total, Japanese names
2. **2D足場図 (SVG)** — Per-wall 2D assembly view with print/PDF/DXF export
3. **3D足場図 (Three.js)** — Interactive 3D view with polygon layout

## Input Modes (3 sections on scaffold/page.tsx)

### 1. AI Extraction (AI抽出)
- Upload image (PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF/BMP), PDF, or DXF
- AI (Claude Vision via Anthropic SDK) analyzes drawing and extracts:
  - Building exterior footprint polygon (vertices)
  - Wall dimensions (wallLengthsMm)
  - Building height (buildingHeightMm)
  - Drawing type, scale, confidence score
  - Obstacles (doors, balconies, AC units, pillars)
- **Backend Service**: [vision-bim.service.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/vision-bim/vision-bim.service.ts)
- **Backend Controller**: [vision-bim.controller.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/vision-bim/vision-bim.controller.ts)
- **API**: `POST /api/v1/vision-bim/analyze` (multipart file upload)
- **API Client**: [vision-bim.ts](mdc:frontend/lib/api/vision-bim.ts)
- Requires `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable
- IFC/BIM files are NOT supported (removed)
- PDF files are converted to images via Sharp before AI analysis
- DXF files are parsed deterministically (no AI needed)
- Silent fallbacks are NOT used — errors are thrown clearly

### 2. File Upload (ファイルアップロード)
- Upload dimensioned drawings for manual extraction
- Uses DrawingUpload component with DXF client-side parsing
- Also supports Quick Shape Builder for simple shapes

### 3. Manual CAD Drawing (手描きCAD)
- AutoCAD-like canvas for manually drawing building plans
- **Component**: [cad-drawing-canvas.tsx](mdc:frontend/components/cad-drawing-canvas.tsx)
- Features: polyline tool, rectangle tool, snap-to-grid, zoom/pan
- Calibration: set known real-world distance for auto-scale
- Dimension editing: click any edge to enter exact mm length
- On complete: generates vertices + wall inputs for scaffold calculation

## Material Breakdown (材料明細)
- **Component**: [material-breakdown-table.tsx](mdc:frontend/components/material-breakdown-table.tsx)
- Per-floor, per-side breakdown of all scaffold materials
- Expandable rows showing quantities at each floor level for each wall
- Editable pricing: click unit price to enter cost per material
- Auto-calculates total cost from quantities × prices
- Shows on result page under "材料明細" tab

## User Management & Authentication

### User Roles
- **admin**: Full access, can manage users
- **estimator**: Can create/edit estimates
- **viewer**: Read-only access

### User Management
- **Backend**: [auth.service.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.ts) - `createUser`, `listUsers`, `updateUser`, `adminResetPassword`, `deactivateUser`
- **Controller**: [auth.controller.ts](mdc:backend/src/modules/auth/auth.controller.ts)
- **Frontend Admin UI**: [users/page.tsx](mdc:frontend/app/users/page.tsx)
- **Frontend Profile**: [profile/page.tsx](mdc:frontend/app/profile/page.tsx)
- **API Client**: [users.ts](mdc:frontend/lib/api/users.ts)
- **Endpoints**:
  - `GET /api/v1/auth/profile` - Get current user
  - `PUT /api/v1/auth/profile` - Update own profile
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/change-password` - Change own password
  - `GET /api/v1/auth/users` - List users (admin)
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/users` - Create user (admin)
  - `PUT /api/v1/auth/users/:id` - Update user (admin)
  - `POST /api/v1/auth/users/:id/reset-password` - Reset password (admin)
  - `DELETE /api/v1/auth/users/:id` - Deactivate user (admin)

